{"meta":{"ticker":"SCHG","as_of_date":"2026-09-18","performance_as_of":"2026-08-31","generated_at":"2026-09-21 19:41:17"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"SCHG","fund_name":"Schwab U.S. Large-Cap Growth ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Growth","issuer":"Charles Schwab","index_name":"Dow Jones US Total Stock Market Large-Cap Growth","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0004,"aum":65888239225,"holdings_count":196,"inception_date":"2009-12-11","overall_score":8.99782743362832,"overall_rank":88,"sector_diversification_score":5.63070662782666},"description":{"tsi_description":"SCHG is a large-cap growth ETF that targets U.S. companies with strong earnings growth, sales growth, and momentum-oriented characteristics. The fund tracks the Dow Jones U.S. Large-Cap Growth Total Stock Market Index and intentionally emphasizes companies with high valuations and low dividend yields. Its market-cap-weighted structure results in significant exposure to mega-cap technology and growth stocks, which has historically contributed to strong long-term returns and quality metrics. Compared to many equal-weight growth strategies, SCHG maintains heavier allocations to larger and more profitable companies, resulting in stronger portfolio-level profitability characteristics. Overall, SCHG offers concentrated exposure to high-quality U.S. growth stocks with substantial long-term growth potential.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the Dow Jones U.S. Large-Cap Growth Total Stock Market Index.","Selects U.S. large-cap stocks with growth-oriented characteristics.","Screens for high projected P/E ratios and high historical price-to-book ratios.","Screens for high projected three-to-five-year operating EPS growth.","Screens for high trailing five-year annualized sales growth.","Screens for high 21-quarter annualized EPS growth.","Screens for low indicated dividend yields.","Uses a float-adjusted market-capitalization weig